From: PonWrt developers <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] debug: restore valid nested WED diagnostic patch

Regenerate the nested diagnostic patch from the actual 0022 output so its
hunk ranges and embedded source are consistent.

Signed-off-by: PonWrt developers <noreply@localhost>
---
diff --git a/target/linux/airoha/patches-6.18/950-net-airoha-record-wed-first-error-and-txfree.patch b/target/linux/airoha/patches-6.18/950-net-airoha-record-wed-first-error-and-txfree.patch
--- a/target/linux/airoha/patches-6.18/950-net-airoha-record-wed-first-error-and-txfree.patch
+++ b/target/linux/airoha/patches-6.18/950-net-airoha-record-wed-first-error-and-txfree.patch
@@ -1,15 +1,9 @@
 From: PonWrt developers <noreply@localhost>
-Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: capture first WED token and coherent errors
+Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: capture WED diagnostics with valid hunk ranges
 
-Count each extended error bit independently of console ratelimiting.
-Keep separate bounded snapshots for missing-payload and RX coherent
-events before W1C acknowledgment. Record native and shadow ring
-positions and allocated coherent descriptors without following DMA
-pointers or changing hardware state. Hardware-owned snapshots can move.
-
-Decode bounded CPU-owned TX-free notifications supplied by mt76 and
-save the preceding and following host views. Expose records through a
-root-readable debugfs file, retaining existing error logs and masks.
+Refresh the generated WED diagnostic patch after expanding the bounded
+TX-free record and attaching follow-up token candidates. Keep the inner
+patch syntactically valid so build-time patch checks can apply it.
 
 Signed-off-by: PonWrt developers <noreply@localhost>
 ---
